  "question": {
    "text": "The number of chiral alcohol(s) with molecular&nbsp;formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is ________ (Assume stereoisomers as different chiral alcohols)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molecular formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Degree of unsaturation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Possible alcohols are:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0187_8b5dcf0f8e13.png\" style=\"width: 496px; height: 82px;\" /></p><p>2-butanol exhibits optical isomerism, hence, two stereoisomers need to be considered.</p>"
  }
